        "date": "2026-11-08T23:12:49Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(import): read named tool coordinate systems from a vendor STEP\n\nA vendor tool STEP package can carry the ISO/TS 13399 3D-model\ncoordinate systems (PCS, MCS, CIP, CSIF, CSW / CSWx / CSWx_y), names\nconfirmed from the public ISO/TS 13399-303, -401 and -405 preview pages.\ngeometry::import::step_csys::read_tool_csys returns every named\nAXIS2_PLACEMENT_3D as plain data (origin in mm by the file's length\nunit, unit z and x), classified by those names. A file without them\ngives a named fall-back reason; a degenerate, non-finite or ambiguous\nplacement is refused by name, never a panic.\n\nReader only: placing a body by these frames waits for #368's tool-body\nmodel. Pinned by the tool_csys suite and three hand-written fixtures.\n\nRefs #370\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
